          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "spēs is inherited, usually traced to Proto-Indo-European speh1-, \"to prosper, to turn out well\" (EtymDB 2.1). prosperus, \"favourable\", and English speed, which once meant \"success\", are often given as cousins."
